{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.WritheIndependenceCriterion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.WritheIndependenceCriterion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.injective_writhe_map_is_falsified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.injective_writhe_map_is_falsified","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheIndependenceCriterion.lean#L88-L102","doc":"**What the p/n test actually establishes.**\n\nNo *injective* function of the writhe can assign the proton and neutron the\nsame hypercharge, since their writhes differ.  This is the honest content of\nthe published argument: it falsifies the linear/injective map `Y = c·w` (the\nframing phase `q^{w·c}`), not every function of `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.pn_test_admits_writhe_only_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.pn_test_admits_writhe_only_map","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheIndependenceCriterion.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**The p/n test admits a writhe-only map.**\n\nWith the derived framing writhes `w(p) = +2`, `w(n) = −2`, the map\n`Y = w²/4` returns `+1` on both.  So `Y(p) = Y(n) = +1` at distinct writhes\nis *consistent* with `Y` being a function of the writhe alone, and cannot by\nitself force a second invariant independent of it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}